  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish that temperature can activate diffusion and structural changes in HEAs, that nanoscale HEA behavior can be studied by molecular dynamics, that free surfaces and surface energy affect nanoscale transformations, and that thermal processing can cause composition-dependent elemental loss or surface-layer formation. R9 is compositionally close and examines temperature effects by MD, while R1 and R6 supply nanoscale surface-energy and shape-reorientation concepts. However, none describes heating AuCoCuNiPt nanoparticles under vacuum or predicts Au/Cu surface segregation followed by evaporation, coalescence, and spherical reshaping. Combining the records points generally toward a thermal nanoscale study, but identifying low-surface-energy segregation and evaporation as the controlling kinetic mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
